  "answer": "Project Zenith is a cloud storage optimization initiative launched in Q3 2023, led by Marcus Cole, with a kickoff meeting on July 15th. The project aims to enhance security, accessibility, and data visualization using AI. Key phases include design, development (led by Omar Jensen), and predictive analytics breakthroughs. The executive board approved a total budget of $2 million, with specific allocations including $550,000 for general project expenses, $55,000 for compliance (training and audits), and $15,000 for specialized team training. Recent updates highlight progress in phase two, with a detailed report due on November 20th, and a request for stakeholder feedback on the prototype by the end of November."
